      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-5",
        "notes": "Reviewed Statement, F1-F2 and Proof 1.1-2.1 against complete published coordinate-contraction supplier proof. Coordinate-pair swap handles either sign of offsets; finite initial subclasses pass to finite signwise suprema without measure convergence. Specified H0 must determine BOTH raw and transformed suprema for every sign vector, so countable reduction is exact. L=0 gives constant coordinate maps and zero transformed sign average; singleton and m=1 cases are sound. Mohri Lemma5.7 pp.93-94 states factor L without Phi(0)=0, but multiplicative (1-epsilon)sup approximation fails for negative suprema; accepted reader annotation correction avoids claiming a complete source proof. Local supplier proof avoids that gap. B&M Theorem12(4) p.469 is only a convention comparison (absolute 2/m, Phi(0)=0, factor2L). No mathematical interface changed; no consumer repair, AC or diagram needed."
