        "notes": "Read complete Statement, A1/F1-F5 and Proof1.1-3.1, plus all six actual supplier interfaces. Bounded measurable suprema on finite probability products are integrable; Fubini applies with sigma-finite factors. Pointwise domination gives sup E<=E sup without selecting maximizers or AC. Product-law rectangle uniqueness makes each pair swap invariant, and finite sign averaging plus subadditivity gives exactly 2 times the nonabsolute 1/m complexity. Negative intermediate suprema cause no problem. Nonempty class and m>=1, singleton/constant losses, and m=1 check. Mohri Theorem3.3 proof pp.31-33 and B&M Theorem8 proof pp.466-468 were compared while keeping their conventions distinct. No tail bound or iff claimed; no diagram or missing supplier."
