      "finite_checks": [],
      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-5",
        "notes": "Read full Statement, A1/F1-F7, all six proof steps, contract citations/derivations and exact eight supplier interfaces; also read McDiarmid full proof. Stated AC is inherited precisely from its conditional-expectation/Hoeffding route; no selector is claimed. Coordinate sample lies on P^m, all named suprema are product-measurable, bounded and integrable; both deviation and empirical complexity have pointwise coordinate oscillation <=1/m, so V=1/m>0 even when actual variation is zero. For 0<delta<1 all logarithms/thresholds are positive and exp(-2mt²)=delta. Complement class remains [0,1], has exactly equal empirical/expected complexity by sign symmetry, and reverses deviation. Checked separate-event semantics and each union allocation: log1/delta; empirical one-sided 3sqrt(log2/delta); expected two-sided sqrt(log2/delta); empirical two-sided 3sqrt(log4/delta). Singleton, constant/zero losses and m=1 are sound; delta endpoints are excluded. Mohri Theorem3.3 proof pp.31-33 confirms the adopted constants; B&M remains a comparison in its different convention. No diagrams, iff, substantive prerequisite gap or repair."
      }
